        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF150Relnote: Document.caretRangeFromPoint() supported]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43591</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43591"/>
        <updated>2026-03-27T13:45:52.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF150 supports <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretRangeFromPoint" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate"> Document.caretRangeFromPoint()</code></a>. This is non-standard, so primarily for parity reasons.<br>
Developers should prefer <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/caretPositionFromPoint" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">caretPositionFromPoint()</code></a> when supported "generally" because it is shadow root aware (but not on FF, which doesn't support the option according to BCD).</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds a release note, and also updates the docs to explain why you should prefer <code class="notranslate">caretPositionFromPoint()</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4127666989" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43550/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43550">#43550</a></p>]]></content>
